WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:03.900
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.140
Steve Carell here.
我是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.500
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

4
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.640
Angela and Jenna, my good, dear, wonderful friends,
安吉拉和珍娜，我亲爱又出色的好朋友，

5
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.140
told me that they are doing a show on all things Michael Scott.
告诉我她们正在做一档关于迈克尔·斯科特一切的节目。

6
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.340
So I thought I should say hello, welcome you to the show,
所以我心想我应该打个招呼，欢迎大家收听节目，

7
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.300
and also congratulate the Office Ladies on Office Ladies 6.0.
并祝贺《办公室女士》进入6.0版本。

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.500
Let us begin with the Michael Scott episode.
让我们从迈克尔·斯科特这一集开始吧。

9
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:30.580
Enjoy.
尽情享受吧。

10
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:30.660
Enjoy.
尽情享受吧。

11
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.820
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.220
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

13
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.080
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

14
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.200
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你们打造了终极《办公室》粉丝播客。

15
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.700
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

16
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.880
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节以及许多闺蜜间的故事。

17
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.920
We're the Office Ladies 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0。

18
00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.160
Oh, hi.
噢，嗨。

19
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.440
How adorable is Steve Carell?
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔是不是太可爱了？

20
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.140
Love him.
超爱他。

21
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.300
He's so sweet.
他真是太贴心了。

22
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:04.540
Just love him.
就是超爱他。

23
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.760
He said a special hello to everybody today.
他今天特意向大家问好。

24
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.640
He sure did.
他确实这么做了。

25
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.640
Well, today on Office Ladies 6.0, as Steve said, it's all about Michael Scott.
好了，今天在《办公室女士》6.0，正如史蒂夫所说，主题是迈克尔·斯科特。

26
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.820
And we got a lot of great mail from you guys on this one.
关于这一集，我们收到了很多你们寄来的精彩邮件。

27
00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.440
I am so excited about some of the things we uncovered about Michael.
我对我们挖掘出的一些关于迈克尔的事情感到非常兴奋。

28
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.560
Jenna has been so secretive.
珍娜一直神神秘秘的。

29
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.520
Can I just tell you?
我能说吗？

30
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.440
She's clearly got some nugget.
她显然掌握了什么猛料。

31
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.660
She won't even tell me or hint about it.
她甚至连暗示都不肯给我。

32
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.040
And, lady, you got to share.
嘿，女士，你得分享一下。

33
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:29.920
I will.
我会的。

34
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:31.700
I will?
我会吗？

35
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.760
Today is the day you find out.
今天就是你揭晓答案的日子。

36
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.900
I just have to wait.
我只能等着。

37
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.460
But first, I think we need to reveal our new format for Office Ladies 6.0.
但首先，我觉得我们需要公布《办公室女士》6.0的新形式。

38
00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.560
This is important.
这很重要。

39
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.080
For me, it is.
对我来说很重要。

40
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:44.660
It is.
确实如此。

41
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.340
Instead of doing fast facts, we are going to start our episodes with a top-of-show share.
我们不再做“快速事实”环节，而是以“开场分享”开启我们的节目。

42
00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.120
Jenna is very happy to ditch fast facts, y'all.
珍娜很高兴能抛弃“快速事实”，伙计们。

43
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:54.920
I really am.
我确实很高兴。

44
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.700
But I still need my structure.
但我还是需要我的结构。

45
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.060
You still need an outline.
你还是需要一份大纲。

46
00:01:59.500 --> 00:01:59.780
Okay.
好吧。

47
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:08.920
So, a top-of-show share can be office news, office ladies news, personal news, or a fan mail share.
所以，“开场分享”可以是办公室新闻、《办公室女士》新闻、个人新闻，或是粉丝来信分享。

48
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.320
So, there's lots of options.
选择有很多。

49
00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:10.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

50
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.780
Today, we have office news and a fan mail share.
今天，我们有办公室新闻和粉丝来信分享。

51
00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:15.660
Yeah.
没错。

52
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.000
Why don't I start?
不如由我来开头吧？

53
00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:17.780
Do it.
请讲。

54
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.000
It's official.
消息确凿。

55
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.600
Office Ladies is going to the paper.
《办公室女士》要进驻《纸媒》剧组了。

56
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.360
Yes, we are visiting Greg Daniels' new show, The Paper.
没错，我们要去探访格雷格·丹尼尔斯的新剧《纸媒》。

57
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.200
We're going to be on the set, lady.
我们要去拍摄现场了，女士。

58
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.000
They are in production right now.
他们现在正在制作中。

59
00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.200
They have been very protective of things leaking out.
他们对消息外泄防范得非常严。

60
00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:33.620
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

61
00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.360
It's locked down.
封锁得很严。

62
00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.040
But we've been invited to visit.
但我们受邀去探班。

63
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:36.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

64
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.320
They said we could bring a little portable recording thingy.
他们说我们可以带个小型的便携录音设备。

65
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.540
Jenna is right now with her hands motioning to her imaginary little microphone.
珍娜现在正用手比划着她那虚构的小麦克风。

66
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.720
Like a little microphone.
就像个小麦克风一样。

67
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:47.700
Yeah.
没错。

68
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.620
Ah, I'm taking it out of my closet, and I'm bringing it to the set of The Paper.
啊，我要把它从壁橱里拿出来，带到《纸媒》的拍摄现场去。

69
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.240
We're going to meet the caSt.
我们要去见见演员阵容。

70
00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.580
We're going to be reunited with so many of our crew.
我们要和许多老同事重聚了。

71
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.820
So much of our crew is working on The Paper.
我们剧组有好多人都在《纸媒》工作。

72
00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.960
We're going to see Veda, our script supervisor.
我们要去见我们的场记维达。

73
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.800
Kelly Cantley and Rusty Mahmood are the first ADs.
凯利·坎特利和拉斯蒂·马哈茂德是第一副导演。

74
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.080
Yeah.
没错。

75
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.320
Ben Patrick is the sound mixer.
本·帕特里克是混音师。

76
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.840
And there are so many fun people from The Office who have been directing episodes of The Paper.
还有好多《办公室》的老朋友在执导《纸媒》的剧集。

77
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.060
Jen Salata.
珍·萨拉塔。

78
00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.340
Ken Quapis.
肯·夸皮斯。

79
00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.420
Jeff Blitz.
杰夫·布里茨。

80
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.580
Matt Sohn.
马特·索恩。

81
00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.880
And the week we're visiting, guess who's directing?
而且我们探班的那一周，你猜是谁在执导？

82
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.500
Dave Rogers!
戴夫·罗杰斯！

83
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.460
Yes!
没错！

84
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.140
Dave Rogers is also a co-executive producer and an editor on the show.
戴夫·罗杰斯同时还是该剧的联合执行制片人和剪辑师。

85
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.140
And directing.
还要负责执导。

86
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.960
That's triple threat right there.
那真是三项全能啊。

87
00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:33.960
It sure is.
确实如此。

88
00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:38.760
And, you know, Paul has been in the writer's room, so we might get to see him too.
而且，你知道，保罗一直在编剧室，所以我们可能也能见到他。

89
00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.060
I just can't wait.
我简直等不及了。

90
00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.500
I'm so excited about it.
我对此太兴奋了。

91
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.600
I think it's going to feel like a mini reunion.
我觉得这会像是一场小型重聚。

92
00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.960
I think it's going to be emotional.
我觉得会很感人。

93
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.360
Oh, for sure.
噢，那肯定的。

94
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.320
But, I mean, we get emotional a lot over things like this.
不过，我是说，我们经常会为这种事感到动容。

95
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:50.780
We do.
确实。

96
00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.020
Why not?
为什么不呢？

97
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.720
This is like our favorite thing.
这可是我们最喜欢的事情之一。

98
00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.640
Well, there you have it.
好了，消息就是这样。

99
00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.500
That's our office news.
这就是我们的办公室新闻。

100
00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.280
Angela?
安吉拉？

101
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.420
Well, my top of show share is inspired by this fan question from Erica H.
嗯，我开场的分享灵感来自于埃里卡·H（Erica H.）发来的粉丝提问。

102
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.460
in Portland, Oregon.
她来自俄勒冈州的波特兰。

103
00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.900
Erica wrote in and said, is there a story to the origin of Michael Scott's name?
埃里卡写信问，迈克尔·斯科特（Michael Scott）这个名字的由来有什么故事吗？

104
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.600
There is a Michael Scott in Dante's Inferno, and I wondered if that inspired anyone in naming the character.
但丁的《神曲·地狱篇》里有个叫迈克尔·斯科特的人，我很好奇这是否启发了角色的命名。

105
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.300
Ooh, I love this question.
噢，我喜欢这个问题。

106
00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:19.020
I know.
我也是。

107
00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.200
So, I reached out to Greg Daniels.
所以我联系了格雷格·丹尼尔斯（Greg Daniels）。

108
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.840
It is not from Dante's Inferno.
并不是出自《神曲·地狱篇》。

109
00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:23.360
Okay.
好吧。

110
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:29.260
So, as you know, on the British show, the manager's name is David Brent, which is two first names.
如你们所知，在英版剧中，经理的名字叫大卫·布伦特（David Brent），那是两个名字。

111
00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.300
And that has become sort of a tradition in the various versions of the office.
这在《办公室》的各个版本中已经成为了一种传统。

112
00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:33.760
Yeah.
没错。

113
00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:39.320
But I was curious, how did Greg settle on the two names, Michael and Scott?
但我很好奇，格雷格是怎么定下“迈克尔”和“斯科特”这两个名字的？

114
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.040
He said this,
他是这么说的：

115
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:49.420
My name is almost two first names, and there is something kind of lame I always felt in a funny way about having two first names and no last name.
我的名字几乎就是两个名字，我一直觉得有两个名字而没有姓氏，在某种程度上挺逊的，也挺好笑的。

116
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.000
And Michael is a pretty generic name for our age group.
而且迈克尔在我们这个年龄段是个很普通的名字。

117
00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.700
There are a ton of Michaels.
叫迈克尔的人多得是。

118
00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:59.720
And I knew a guy named Scott, who was kind of a derp, so I just put them together.
我认识一个叫斯科特的人，他有点呆头呆脑的，所以我就把这两个名字拼在一起了。

119
00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:05.810
Derp.
呆头呆脑。

120
00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:06.270
I know.
我知道。

121
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.650
I have never heard that.
我从来没听说过这个。

122
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.270
So, there you go, Erica.
所以，这就是答案，埃里卡。

123
00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.070
That is how Greg Daniels came up with the name Michael Scott.
这就是格雷格·丹尼尔斯想出迈克尔·斯科特这个名字的过程。

124
00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:18.450
Well, my husband, Lee Kirk, has two first names.
嗯，我丈夫李·柯克（Lee Kirk）就有两个名字。

125
00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:22.530
And I can tell you, it causes him a lot of grief.
我可以告诉你，这让他很苦恼。

126
00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.550
We've talked about this.
我们聊过这个。

127
00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:32.310
I texted Greg back, and I said, You know, Greg, Jenna and I have talked about the fact that Lee has two first names, Lee Kirk.
我给格雷格回了短信，我说，你知道吗，格雷格，我和珍娜聊过李有两个名字这件事，李·柯克。

128
00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:37.130
And Greg responded with the emoji that's the two exclamation points.
格雷格回了一个两个感叹号的表情符号。

129
00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:44.770
I mean, I can't tell you how many dinner reservations, hotel reservations, where people call him Mr. Lee.
我是说，我数不清有多少次预订晚餐或酒店时，人们管他叫李先生。

130
00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:45.970
Yes.
是的。

131
00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.270
Mr. Lee, welcome.
李先生，欢迎光临。

132
00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.650
We don't correct people anymore.
我们现在都不纠正别人了。

133
00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:50.570
You just go with it.
你就顺着他们说吧。

134
00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:50.990
We do.
我们确实是这样。

135
00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:51.510
I know.
我知道。

136
00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.850
It's like me and Kingsley.
就像我和金斯利（Kingsley）一样。

137
00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.850
I'm just going to say, okay, sure.
我只会说，好的，没问题。

138
00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:55.330
Yep.
没错。

139
00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.330
Well, finally, we have some office ladies news.
好了，最后，我们有一些《办公室》女士们的新闻。

140
00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.210
Yeah.
是啊。

141
00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.910
So, I guess this would be our third thing.
所以，我想这应该是我们的第三件事了。

142
00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.750
Oh, my God.
天哪。

143
00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.970
We just did fast facts.
我们刚刚才做完快速事实。

144
00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:05.950
We kind of did.
算是吧。

145
00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.770
You can't get away from it, Jenna.
你逃不掉的，珍娜。

146
00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.130
What the hell?
搞什么鬼？

147
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:10.290
Angela.
安吉拉。

148
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.510
H-E-double hockey sticks.
见鬼去吧。

149
00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:14.810
Well.
好吧。

150
00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.570
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

151
00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.090
I actually can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

152
00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.690
I – okay.
我——好吧。

153
00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:19.670
Well –
嗯——

154
00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.090
You know what?
你知道吗？

155
00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:23.710
I'm going to just say, I bet it's not the last time you do fast facts.
我只想说，我敢打赌这绝对不是你最后一次做快速问答了。

156
00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:24.730
I'm just saying it.
我只是随口一说。

157
00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.230
Why would you say that?
你为什么要这么说？

158
00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.950
You're saying it like, what?
你这话说的，是什么意思？

159
00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.130
I want to be rid of these.
我想摆脱这些。

160
00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.410
I've just jinxed you.
我刚才乌鸦嘴了。

161
00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:32.870
Okay.
好吧。

162
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.930
Well, we had a super fun trip.
总之，我们度过了一次超级愉快的旅行。

163
00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.250
We were going to share about it.
我们本来打算分享一下的。

164
00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:42.350
We went up to Santa Barbara, and we finally got to meet in person Kendra Adachi, the lazy genius.
我们去了圣巴巴拉，终于见到了“懒人天才”肯德拉·阿达奇本人。

165
00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:49.970
Yes, she was the keynote speaker at an event that weekend, but we got to have a very girly, fun lunch with her.
没错，那个周末她是活动的特邀演讲嘉宾，但我们还是和她一起吃了一顿非常开心、充满少女心的午餐。

166
00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:56.110
We took pictures, and then Angela and I decided to stay over.
我们拍了照片，然后安吉拉和我决定留宿。

167
00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:06.110
We really wanted to mark the occasion of five years of office ladies with a really luxurious work trip as a reward for ourselves.
我们真的很想用一次极其奢华的工作旅行来纪念《办公室女郎》五周年，作为对我们自己的奖励。

168
00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:06.710
We did.
我们确实这么做了。

169
00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:10.790
We treated ourselves, and we also, though, had an amazing work session.
我们犒劳了自己，而且我们也进行了一场非常棒的工作会议。

170
00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:11.790
We did.
确实如此。

171
00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.370
I mean, that's very much like us, but it was so fun from the beginning.
我是说，这很像我们的风格，但从一开始就非常有趣。

172
00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.530
We drove up together.
我们是一起开车上去的。

173
00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:22.570
Angela drove, and I did get nauseous, but it's not your fault, Ange.
安吉拉开车，我确实晕车了，但这不怪你，安吉。

174
00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.970
I really tried not to take any turns too faSt.
我真的尽量不转弯太快。

175
00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:33.970
You did such a good job, but, you know, with the medicines that I'm taking, they just cause a low level of baseline nausea.
你做得很好，但是你知道，我吃的那些药会引起轻微的持续性恶心。

176
00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:42.810
I pretty much feel like I walk through life with, like, first trimester morning sickness all the time, but it gets really triggered in vehicles.
我感觉自己就像一直处于怀孕前三个月的晨吐状态，但在车里这种感觉会被加剧。

177
00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.830
You travel with your saltine crackers everywhere you go.
你走到哪儿都带着苏打饼干。

178
00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:50.350
With a sleeve of saltine crackers and ginger juice.
带着一整筒苏打饼干和姜汁。

179
00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:57.810
I have to tell you, when I got back, I had to pick up the kids from school, and Josh was going to ride with me, and he said,
我得告诉你，我回来后去学校接孩子，乔什要坐我的车，他说，

180
00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.650
What happened in your passenger seat?
你的副驾驶座上发生了什么？

181
00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:00.570
What did they were?
那都是些什么碎屑？

182
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.850
They're all kinds of crops.
到处都是饼干碎。

183
00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.410
I'm so sorry.
真抱歉。

184
00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:08.750
I said, poor Jenna ate probably a sleeve of saltine crackers in the car.
我说，可怜的珍娜在车里大概吃了一整筒苏打饼干。

185
00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.290
I really tried not to be swervy, lady.
我真的尽量不乱晃了，女士。

186
00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.410
I hope I'm sorry.
我希望……我很抱歉。

187
00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:12.870
You were great.
你开得很好。

188
00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:13.630
You were great.
你开得很好。

189
00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:21.310
But what was really cool was we went to this hotel that was on the beach, but we had booked garden rooMs.
但真正酷的是，我们去的那家酒店就在海滩边，但我们预订的是花园房。

190
00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:27.510
But when we checked in, they upgraded us to on the beach.
可当我们办理入住时，他们把我们升级到了海景房。

191
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.690
Jenna started to cry.
珍娜开始哭了。

192
00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:29.610
I did cry.
我确实哭了。

193
00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:34.650
You were so excited because we had talked about how we'd love to stay on the beach, but we're like, no, it's...
你当时太激动了，因为我们之前聊过想住海滩边，但我们觉得，不，这……

194
00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.170
It was a little extravagant.
这有点太奢侈了。

195
00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:38.170
It was, like, pricey, and we're like, we'll just stay.
确实挺贵的，我们当时想，还是住花园房吧。

196
00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.150
I love a garden.
我喜欢花园。

197
00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.430
I love a garden nook.
我喜欢花园角落。

198
00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.810
And then we got the upgrade, and that was so fun.
然后我们得到了升级，那真的太棒了。

199
00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:55.090
And I got to wake up to the ocean right there, and we took walks on the beach, and we worked, and then we had a big celebration dinner that I forced us to have.
我醒来就能看到大海，我们在海滩上散步，工作，然后还吃了一顿我强行要求安排的盛大庆祝晚餐。

200
00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.250
I'm sorry, Angela.
对不起，安吉拉。

201
00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.650
I love a tasting menu.
我喜欢品鉴菜单。

202
00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:00.590
She does.
她确实喜欢。

203
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.330
And you guys, I don't do tasting menus.
但伙计们，我不怎么吃品鉴菜单。

204
00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:03.930
I don't...
我不太……

205
00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.870
I mean, I just don't know much about them.
我是说，我对那玩意儿不太了解。

206
00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:08.510
And it was eight courses.
而且那是八道菜。

207
00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:09.910
Of seafood.
全是海鲜。

208
00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:10.970
Of seafood.
全是海鲜。

209
00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.350
And it was really good.
味道确实很好。

210
00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.750
It was really good, but by the end, I said, I can't do it anymore.
味道真的很好，但吃到最后，我说，我实在吃不下了。

211
00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:16.270
Yeah.
是啊。

212
00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:20.430
Although then they wheeled out a cheese cart, and you said, I will take some of that.
虽然之后他们推出来一辆奶酪车，你就说，我要来点那个。

213
00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:21.210
Okay, fine.
好吧，行吧。

214
00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.150
I mean, you had me at cheese cart.
我是说，奶酪车一出，我就被俘获了。

215
00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:23.730
Yeah.
是啊。

216
00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:29.810
But the coolest thing during the dinner, I think, was when they brought out that bread, Ange.
但我觉得晚餐最棒的部分，是他们端上那款面包的时候，安吉。

217
00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:38.750
And it was this sourdough bread with a starter that was, like, 30 years old that the chef travels the world with.
那是一种酸种面包，用的酵母种有30年历史了，主厨带着它周游世界。

218
00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:41.010
He travels the world with his starter.
他带着他的酵母种周游世界。

219
00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.590
You know I loved that.
你知道我有多喜欢那个。

220
00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.710
Your eyes about fell out of your head.
你的眼珠子都快掉出来了。

221
00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:52.410
And there were, like, flavored butters, like a butter infused with seaweed that I wasn't sure about but was really good.
还有各种风味黄油，比如一种海藻味的黄油，我一开始不太确定，但味道真的很好。

222
00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.150
It was salty.
咸咸的。

223
00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:53.730
Really, really good.
真的，非常好吃。

224
00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:54.770
But, yes.
不过，没错。

225
00:09:54.770 --> 00:10:00.770
Anyway, we had a fantastic trip, and I want you guys to know, Kendra is the real deal.
总之，我们那次旅行棒极了，我想让你们知道，肯德拉是个非常实在的人。

226
00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:05.070
Sitting with her, having lunch with her, I felt like I had known her my whole life.
和她坐在一起，和她共进午餐，我感觉就像认识她一辈子了一样。

227
00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:12.370
She is so warm and just a delight to be around and smart and funny, and that was such a highlight as well.
她非常热情，和她在一起很开心，而且她聪明又风趣，那也是这次旅行的一大亮点。

228
00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:18.370
And we took a bunch of pictures and videos on our work trip, which we never posted because I was nauseous for two days.
我们在出差期间拍了很多照片和视频，但一直没发，因为我恶心了两天。

229
00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:19.970
And then we had no Wi-Fi.
而且当时没Wi-Fi。

230
00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:25.010
We had no Wi-Fi when we got there, and when we got home, I was like, I can't look at a screen anymore.
我们到那儿时没Wi-Fi，等回到家，我就觉得，我再也不想看屏幕了。

231
00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:29.630
So we'll throw them up in Office Ladies Pod finally this week.
所以我们这周终于会把它们发到《办公室女士》播客上了。

232
00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.390
You can check it out.
你们可以去看看。

233
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:30.970
Yeah.
好。

234
00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:34.210
So happy five years and happy getting to meet Kendra.
所以，五周年快乐，能见到肯德拉也很开心。

235
00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:36.950
Well, listen, why don't we take a break?
好了，听着，我们休息一下好吗？

236
00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:44.730
And when we come back, I really did a deep dive on Michael's mangled words and phrases.
回来之后，我会深入挖掘迈克尔那些被说错的词汇和短语。

237
00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:50.090
It is my favorite thing about Michael Scott, and I had so much fun.
这是我最喜欢迈克尔·斯科特的一点，我做得非常开心。

238
00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:55.710
And my favorite thing about Michael Scott is how much he hates technology, and I dive into that.
而我最喜欢迈克尔·斯科特的另一点是他有多讨厌科技，我也会深入探讨这一点。

239
00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:08.030
All right.
好的。

240
00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:08.870
We are back.
我们回来了。

241
00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.390
Let's get started on our Michael Scott breakdown.
让我们开始对迈克尔·斯科特进行深度剖析吧。

242
00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:17.270
I thought we could start by cracking open the show Bible and seeing what all we know about Michael.
我想我们可以先打开剧集设定集，看看我们对迈克尔了解多少。

243
00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:20.910
It's sort of a summary of Michael Scott.
这算是迈克尔·斯科特的人物小传。

244
00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.050
You just had to get a summary, didn't you?
你非得弄个总结不可，是吧？

245
00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:23.350
Did you?
是吗？

246
00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:23.970
You noticed?
你注意到了？

247
00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:24.890
I did notice.
我确实注意到了。

248
00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.450
All right.
好吧。

249
00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:26.870
Here is your summary.
这就是你的总结。

250
00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:36.730
Michael Gary Scott is the regional manager of Dunder Mifflin Scranton, and he believes that the most important thing about a company is the people.
迈克尔·加里·斯科特是邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司的区域经理，他认为公司最重要的就是员工。

251
00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:41.310
He was born at 1123 in the morning and raised in Lackawanna County.
他出生于上午11点23分，在拉卡瓦纳县长大。

252
00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:42.570
1123.
11点23分。

253
00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.910
So specific.
真够具体的。

254
00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:47.970
He grew up on Kenneth Road down the street from Chili's.
他在肯尼斯路长大，离那家辣椒餐厅（Chili's）不远。

255
00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.490
He failed the first grade at least once.
他至少留过一次级，没能升上二年级。

256
00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:58.410
Prior to working at Dunder Mifflin, he worked in a fast food restaurant to save up money for business school, but he lost it in a pyramid scheme.
在邓德·米夫林工作之前，他在一家快餐店打工攒钱准备上商学院，结果钱全被一个传销骗局给骗光了。

257
00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:09.250
So I guess you could say he's a little gullible because he also fell for the Nigerian prince banking email scam and got tricked into thinking there was a sport called poop ball.
所以我猜你可以说他有点容易上当，因为他还信过尼日利亚王子的银行邮件诈骗，还被人骗说有一种运动叫“屎球”。

258
00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:16.250
He also worked as a greeter at Men's Warehouse and invested in Blockbuster.
他还曾在男装仓库（Men's Warehouse）当过迎宾员，还投资过百视达。

259
00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.050
He loves working at Dunder Mifflin, but he is not crazy about the name.
他很喜欢在邓德·米夫林工作，但对这个名字不太感冒。

260
00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:28.010
He thinks it should be called something like Paper Great or Great Papers Are Passion or Super Duper Paper.
他觉得公司应该叫“纸业大亨”、“纸业激情”或者“超级无敌纸业”之类的名字。

261
00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.450
Super Duper Paper is pretty great.
“超级无敌纸业”确实挺棒的。

262
00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:37.510
He would love to start a restaurant called Mike's Cereal Shack or maybe a fancy men's shoe store called Shoe La La.
他很想开一家叫“迈克的麦片小屋”的餐厅，或者一家叫“鞋啦啦”的高档男鞋店。

263
00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:43.110
His heroes are Bob Hope, Abraham Lincoln, Bono, and God.
他的偶像是鲍勃·霍普、亚伯拉罕·林肯、波诺和上帝。

264
00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:49.910
He claims to be part English, Irish, German, Scottish, as well as two-fifteenths Native American.
他自称有英国、爱尔兰、德国、苏格兰血统，还有十五分之二的美国原住民血统。

265
00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:52.310
Michael enjoys improv.
迈克尔喜欢即兴表演。

266
00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.990
He really loves sugar.
他真的很爱吃糖。

267
00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.610
He has milk and sugar in the mornings.
他早上喝牛奶要加糖。

268
00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.010
He adds sugar to his diet cola.
他喝健怡可乐也要加糖。

269
00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.970
He likes scotch and Splenda.
他喜欢苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

270
00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.230
And his favorite drink is grenadine.
他最喜欢的饮料是红石榴糖浆。

271
00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:09.170
That's just the red syrup that you put in a Shirley Temple.
那不就是加在秀兰·邓波儿鸡尾酒里的那种红色糖浆吗？

272
00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.570
Isn't that just like a sweetener flavor?
那难道不是一种调味甜味剂吗？

273
00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:14.970
You don't drink that by itself.
没人会直接喝那个吧。

274
00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:15.810
Michael does.
迈克尔会。

275
00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:16.250
Okay.
好吧。

276
00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.050
He has also been known to stress eat.
众所周知，他压力大时会暴饮暴食。

277
00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:27.530
He likes filet-o'-fish, sausage, egg, and cheese biscuits, bologna, tomato, and ketchup sub-sandwiches.
他喜欢麦香鱼、香肠蛋芝士饼，还有博洛尼亚香肠番茄番茄酱三明治。

278
00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:31.810
He orders the sweet pretzel with the 18 different toppings.
他点甜味椒盐卷饼时会加18种不同的配料。

279
00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.990
He once lived on cup of noodles in college.
大学时他曾靠杯面度日。

280
00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:38.270
And he loves mint chocolate chip ice cream cake.
他还特别喜欢薄荷巧克力碎冰淇淋蛋糕。

281
00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:41.370
He would actually kill himself if he was allergic to dairy.
如果他对乳制品过敏，他真的会自杀的。

282
00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.270
He is, however...
然而，他确实……

283
00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:45.210
He did that in the Alliance.
他在“联盟”那一集里说过。

284
00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.230
He did.
他确实说过。

285
00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:46.610
Yeah.
没错。

286
00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.210
He says it to Meredith when they're eating cake.
那是他和梅雷迪思吃蛋糕时说的。

287
00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:50.870
And she's like, oh, I can't have any.
当时她说，噢，我不能吃。

288
00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:51.930
I'm allergic to dairy.
我对乳制品过敏。

289
00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.950
He is sick of Chuck E.
他受够了查克·E.

290
00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:54.230
Cheese.
芝士餐厅。

291
00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:55.870
And he is not a fan of apricots.
而且他不喜欢杏子。

292
00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:58.490
He plays Who Would You Do?
他玩“你会选谁？”游戏，

293
00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.230
all the time when he's falling asleep.
经常玩到快睡着的时候。

294
00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:03.330
And he loves to wake up to the smell of bacon in the morning.
他喜欢早上在培根的香味中醒来。

295
00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:09.230
He's a fan of the Pittsburgh Pirates, does not like the New York Mets, is a great hockey player,
他是匹兹堡海盗队的粉丝，不喜欢纽约大都会队，是个很棒的曲棍球手，

296
00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.530
but not good at basketball.
但篮球打得不好。

297
00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:16.410
He wears Rite Aid night-swept cologne, which is the perfect smell-alike for Drakkar Noir.
他喷的是Rite Aid买的夜间古龙水，那味道跟Drakkar Noir简直一模一样。

298
00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.050
He loves a party, loves a holiday, loves to dress up as different characters.
他热爱派对，热爱节日，喜欢打扮成各种不同的角色。

299
00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:28.130
He claims to be the king of email forwards, but he doesn't really read memos.
他自称是邮件转发之王，但他其实根本不看备忘录。

300
00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.070
He dry-cleans his jeans.
他洗牛仔裤都要送去干洗。

301
00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:36.930
He claims he can bench-press 190 pounds, but also only works out with two-and-a-half-pound weights.
他声称自己能卧推190磅，但平时只用2.5磅的哑铃锻炼。

302
00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.430
He's a big fan of Fear Factor.
他是《恐惧因素》的忠实粉丝。

303
00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:45.810
He's afraid of being buried alive, but his greatest fear is being alone.
他害怕被活埋，但他最大的恐惧是孤独。

304
00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:49.290
He would love to be part of an inside joke one day.
他梦想有一天能参与到一个内部梗中。

305
00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.530
He enjoys cuddling and spooning.
他喜欢拥抱和依偎在一起。

306
00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.850
He longs for a wife and children.
他渴望拥有妻子和孩子。

307
00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.530
He's good with kids.
他很擅长带孩子。

308
00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:01.750
He keeps a diary, has soft teeth, and has had multiple vasectomies.
他写日记，牙齿很脆弱，还做过好几次输精管结扎手术。

309
00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:05.910
He eventually met the love of his life at work, Holly.
他最终在工作中遇到了他的一生挚爱，霍莉。

310
00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:09.910
They married and moved to Colorado and have two kids.
他们结婚后搬到了科罗拉多州，育有两个孩子。

311
00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.670
Well, I just loved that.
天哪，我太喜欢这个了。

312
00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:16.030
What a wonderfully, like, huge picture we got to see of Michael.
我们看到的迈克尔的形象真是太全面、太宏大了。

313
00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.390
Jenna, you must have worked so hard on that.
珍娜，你一定为此付出了很多努力。

314
00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:21.230
Was that—I mean, I don't know what the show Bible looks like.
那是——我是说，我不知道剧集“圣经”长什么样。

315
00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.470
I haven't ever seen it.
我从来没见过。

316
00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:27.550
The show Bible is just lists of facts about each person.
剧集“圣经”就是关于每个人的事实列表。

317
00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:28.030
Okay.
好吧。

318
00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:35.310
And it starts with season one, episode one, and then it just goes through every episode.
它从第一季第一集开始，然后贯穿每一集。

319
00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:40.590
So you have to go through all the seasons for that one character and compile it all?
所以你必须看完那个角色的所有剧集，然后把它们汇总起来？

320
00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.690
That's what I did.
我就是这么做的。

321
00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.330
Oh, lady.
噢，天哪。

322
00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:43.410
That was a big job.
那可是项大工程。

323
00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.050
Thank you.
谢谢你。

324
00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:44.710
You're welcome.
不客气。

325
00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:46.390
Well, I had a lot of fun doing it.
其实我做的时候挺开心的。

326
00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:51.830
It was pretty cool, but yeah, I mean, I think the section of Michael Scott in the show Bible
这真的很酷，不过，我是说，我觉得剧集“圣经”里迈克尔·斯科特那一章

327
00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:56.830
is something like 14 pages long of facts about Michael Scott.
关于迈克尔·斯科特的事实大概有14页那么长。

328
00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:57.510
Wow.
哇。

329
00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:03.870
You know, he also has the most episodes named after him, Michael Scott.
你知道吗，以他名字命名的剧集也是最多的，就是迈克尔·斯科特。

330
00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:04.550
Oh.
噢。

331
00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.690
Followed by Dwight and then Andy.
其次是德怀特，然后是安迪。

332
00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:13.810
So Michael has six episodes named after him, and Andy and Dwight have three each.
所以迈克尔有六集是以他名字命名的，而安迪和德怀特各有三集。

333
00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.230
That's good trivia, lady.
这冷知识真不错，女士。

334
00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:15.570
Yeah.
是啊。

335
00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.630
I should have hit you up when I made up a quiz.
我做测验的时候应该找你帮忙的。

336
00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.550
I made up a quiz for Michael Scott.
我为迈克尔·斯科特做了一个测验。

337
00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.390
Oh, okay.
噢，好的。

338
00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:25.890
But you might have covered some of it in the show Bible, but I still have a few that are
虽然你可能在剧集“圣经”里涵盖了一些内容，但我还是有几个问题

339
00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:26.790
going to surprise you.
会让你感到惊讶。

340
00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:27.210
Okay.
好的。

341
00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.230
Some deep cut Michael Scott.
一些关于迈克尔·斯科特的冷门知识。

342
00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:29.850
Hmm.
嗯。

343
00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:33.730
Well, I have a fan question, Jenna, I wanted to answer from Michelle M.
珍娜，我有一个来自伯克利的米歇尔·M的粉丝提问想回答。

344
00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:34.470
from Berkeley.
来自伯克利。

345
00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:38.770
She wrote in and said, where did Michael get his dundies?
她写信问，迈克尔的“邓迪奖”是从哪儿来的？

346
00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.270
He created the award.
是他自己创立了这个奖项。

347
00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:43.410
Does this imply he also awarded one to himself?
这是否意味着他也给自己颁过奖？

348
00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.390
Which dundies did he receive?
他都拿过哪些邓迪奖？

349
00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.370
I have always wondered this.
我一直很好奇这一点。

350
00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:52.130
Well, I did some digging, and I read our table read draft of the dundies script, the shooting
嗯，我做了一些调查，读了我们《邓迪奖》那一集的剧本围读草稿，还有拍摄稿

351
00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:52.470
draft.
草稿。

352
00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:53.810
I found some fun stuff.
我发现了一些有趣的东西。

353
00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.650
And then I also reached out to Greg.
然后我还联系了格雷格。

354
00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:56.890
Poor Greg.
可怜的格雷格。

355
00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:58.630
I was just texting him like crazy.
我当时简直是在疯狂地给他发短信。

356
00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.530
I texted Greg like crazy as well.
我也疯狂地给格雷格发了短信。

357
00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:03.230
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

358
00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.910
He's going to be like, ladies, what are you doing?
他肯定会想，女士们，你们在干什么？

359
00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.230
I literally texted one more random question about Michael Scott.
我真的又发了一个关于迈克尔·斯科特的随机问题。

360
00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:09.490
Okay.
好吧。

361
00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.030
Last one.
最后一个。

362
00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:14.950
So, Michelle, to answer your first question, where did Michael go to get his dundies?
那么，米歇尔，回答你的第一个问题，迈克尔去哪儿买的邓迪奖杯？

363
00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.570
I found this scene in the table draft.
我在剧本草稿里找到了这一幕。

364
00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.690
Interior trophy shop.
内景，奖杯店。

365
00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.650
Michael stands at the counter of a trophy shop.
迈克尔站在奖杯店的柜台前。

366
00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:25.250
He points to a dundie man on the shelf.
他指着架子上的一个邓迪小人。

367
00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:27.550
He says, there he is.
他说，就是他。

368
00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.610
Isn't he a handsome son of a bitch?
他难道不是个帅气的混蛋吗？

369
00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.870
The mythical golden dundie man.
传说中的金色邓迪小人。

370
00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.630
The clerk says, it's acrylic laminate.
店员说，那是亚克力层压板做的。

371
00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.790
Michael says, uh-huh.
迈克尔说，嗯哼。

372
00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:36.210
Perfect.
完美。

373
00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:36.550
Okay.
好吧。

374
00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:37.550
I'll take 18, please.
我要18个，谢谢。

375
00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.130
The clerk says, we have none in stock that size.
店员说，那种尺寸的我们没货了。

376
00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.110
I can get 18 of the larger ones.
我可以给你18个大号的。

377
00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:44.430
And then he shows Michael the larger ones.
然后他给迈克尔看了大号的。

378
00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:46.570
They're twice as big, much nicer.
它们大了一倍，好多了。

379
00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.730
And Michael's like, all right, you know what?
迈克尔就说，好吧，你知道吗？

380
00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.790
Yes, sign me up.
行，我要了。

381
00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.970
And then the clerk says, they're $30 each.
然后店员说，每个30美元。

382
00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.550
And Michael's like, okay, well, what else do you have while we're looking?
迈克尔就说，好吧，那我们看看的时候，你还有什么别的？

383
00:17:57.070 --> 00:18:01.830
Then the next scene is Michael at the register, and there are a bunch of smallish trophies.
下一幕是迈克尔在收银台，那里有一堆小一点的奖杯。

384
00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:09.210
The clerk says, okay, we have six swimmers, four football players, three lacrosse girls, and five forensic plaques.
店员说，好的，我们有六个游泳运动员，四个橄榄球运动员，三个长曲棍球女孩，还有五个法医奖牌。

385
00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:10.510
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

386
00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:13.650
And Michael says, gorgeous, do you take diner's club?
迈克尔说，太棒了，你们收大来卡吗？

387
00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:19.210
So there was a scene where he went to a trophy shop, and he went looking for the dundies.
所以确实有一幕是他去了奖杯店，去寻找邓迪奖杯。

388
00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:25.330
And to answer your second question, here's what Greg had to say about how many dundies Michael had.
至于回答你的第二个问题，格雷格对于迈克尔有多少个邓迪奖杯是这样说的。

389
00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:30.250
He said, well, we always had one on his desk, and then Jan throws one at him.
他说，嗯，我们一直让他桌上放一个，然后简扔了一个给他。

390
00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:35.830
And in shareholder meeting, he does say that he's won over 17 dundies.
在股东大会那一集，他确实说过他赢得了超过17个邓迪奖杯。

391
00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.910
The man has a lot of dundies.
这家伙有好多邓迪奖杯。

392
00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.830
So it's clear he's given himself a bunch of awards.
所以很明显，他给自己颁发了一堆奖项。

393
00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:44.950
But as far as what they say, we actually don't ever see one.
但至于上面写了什么，我们其实从来没看清过一个。

394
00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:49.450
I mean, in the beginning credits, he's positioning one at the end of his desk.
我是说，在片头字幕里，他把一个放在办公桌尽头。

395
00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:52.990
But the way the camera crops it, you don't see the little plaque.
但摄像机的取景方式让你看不到上面的小铭牌。

396
00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:53.450
Yep.
没错。

397
00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:58.830
And then in the dundies episode, he holds up a few, but you can't see what's on them.
然后在《邓迪奖》那一集，他举起了几个，但你看不清上面写了什么。

398
00:18:59.150 --> 00:18:59.710
I see.
我明白了。

399
00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:08.230
But Jenna and I both just rewatched the pilot, and we both looked to see if we could see what the plaque says on the dundies.
但珍娜和我刚重温了试播集，我们都想看看能不能看清邓迪奖杯上的铭牌写了什么。

400
00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.470
But the way the camera crops it, we couldn't see it.
但摄像机的取景方式让我们没能看清。

401
00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:10.990
No.
不。

402
00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:13.130
If someone out there saw it, let us know.
如果有人看到了，请告诉我们。

403
00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.270
But we could not see it.
但我们没能看到。

404
00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:18.470
In fact, fan catch, in the pilot, his dundie is on his back credenza.
事实上，粉丝们注意到了，在试播集中，他的邓迪奖杯放在他身后的柜子上。

405
00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:20.230
It's not on his desk.
没在他的办公桌上。

406
00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.350
Like the opening credits.
就像片头字幕里那样。

407
00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.110
That's right.
没错。

408
00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:22.970
Nice, Jenna.
干得好，珍娜。

409
00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:31.330
This is when I really wish that we could reach out to Phil Shea, because I know that he did put something on each one of those plaques.
这时候我真的很希望我们能联系上菲尔·谢伊，因为我知道他在每一块奖牌上都放了东西。

410
00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:33.870
And he could probably tell us what it is.
他大概能告诉我们那是什么。

411
00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:34.310
Yeah.
是啊。

412
00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.810
And so, I miss you, Phil.
所以，菲尔，我想你了。

413
00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:37.830
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:43.990
Well, lady, I thought we could each discuss our favorite thing about Michael Scott.
好吧，女士，我想我们可以各自聊聊迈克尔·斯科特最让我们喜欢的地方。

415
00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:44.630
Okay.
好啊。

416
00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.310
We talked about this.
我们讨论过这个。

