00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:58.730
I have your baguette.
我拿到了你的法棍面包。

457
00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:00.510
And like I'm going to believe one of his sperm lovers.
而且我凭什么要相信他那些精子崇拜者之一的话。

458
00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.730
A day which will live in famously.
这注定是声名狼藉的一天。

459
00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.350
Integral to the story.
对故事至关重要。

460
00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:08.210
We're all successories.
我们都是成功的附属品。

461
00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.050
I forgot about that one.
我把那件事给忘了。

462
00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:21.470
So I think the reason why I love this so much is that initially the character of Michael Scott was based on David Brent from the British office.
我觉得我之所以这么喜欢这个角色，是因为迈克尔·斯科特这个角色最初是以英版《办公室》里的戴维·布伦特为原型的。

463
00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:21.870
Yeah.
没错。

464
00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:25.030
But this character trait is uniquely Michael.
但这个性格特征是迈克尔独有的。

465
00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:28.290
This was not something that was based on the British show.
这并不是基于英版剧集的内容。

466
00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:32.550
And it got me wondering when exactly did we key in on this?
这让我很好奇，我们究竟是什么时候开始关注这一点的？

467
00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.530
Like when did this change happen?
比如这种转变是什么时候发生的？

468
00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:38.950
And the first time that Michael mangles a word is in the pilot.
迈克尔第一次用错词是在试播集中。

469
00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.590
That is when he says incalculable.
就是他说“不可估量”的时候。

470
00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:42.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

471
00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:50.350
So I thought that was really significant because we've talked about how the pilot was basically the pilot script of the British show.
我觉得这意义重大，因为我们讨论过试播集基本上就是英版剧集的剧本。

472
00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:50.730
Yeah.
没错。

473
00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:53.110
But this little detail leaked in.
但这个小细节渗透了进来。

474
00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:56.890
And when we did our breakdown of the pilot, we talked a little bit about this.
当我们分析试播集时，稍微聊过这个。

475
00:21:57.050 --> 00:22:00.990
We said there was this talking head that was brand new to our version.
我们提到过有一个访谈镜头是我们版本独有的。

476
00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:08.350
Greg asked Steve to write down a list of who he thought Michael Scott would consider his heroes.
格雷格让史蒂夫列出一份他认为迈克尔·斯科特会视为英雄的人物名单。

477
00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:13.870
And that's when he lists all the people and he goes on to talk about their contributions to the world.
然后他列出了所有人，并开始谈论他们对世界的贡献。

478
00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:15.850
And then he said incalculable.
接着他说了“不可估量”。

479
00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:16.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

480
00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:18.970
Well, I asked Greg about that.
我问过格雷格这件事。

481
00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:22.670
And he said Steve came up with that on the day.
他说那是史蒂夫当天想出来的。

482
00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:28.490
Just on the day in one of his takes, he throws out this mangled word.
就在拍摄当天的某次录制中，他随口抛出了这个用错的词。

483
00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:39.910
And I just love this so much because I feel like we can credit Greg's collaborative spirit, Steve Carell's amazing improvisation.
我太喜欢这个细节了，因为我觉得这要归功于格雷格的合作精神和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔惊人的即兴发挥。

484
00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:43.990
And it gave birth to this whole character trait.
这催生了整个角色特征。

485
00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:44.490
Yes.
是的。

486
00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:47.990
It reminds me so much of how a Post-it note led to Sprinkles.
这让我想起了便利贴是如何引出“斯普林克尔斯”这个梗的。

487
00:22:48.210 --> 00:22:48.350
Yeah.
没错。

488
00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:48.890
Right?
对吧？

489
00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:53.670
Well, you know, eventually we started writing to this.
你知道，后来我们开始专门为这个特点进行创作。

490
00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:54.150
Yeah.
没错。

491
00:22:54.150 --> 00:23:01.710
And I got very curious if there was someone in the writer's room who specialized in these because they show up in so many episodes.
我很好奇编剧室里是否有人专门负责这些词，因为它们在太多剧集中出现了。

492
00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:03.990
So I did a major deep dive.
所以我做了一次深度挖掘。

493
00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:10.950
Thanks to Dunderpedia, they have a list of every single word or phrase Michael has gotten wrong divided up per episode.
多亏了Dunderpedia，他们列出了迈克尔在每一集中用错的所有词汇或短语。

494
00:23:11.190 --> 00:23:11.610
Wow.
哇。

495
00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:15.370
In most episodes, he has one or none.
在大多数剧集中，他只会用错一个或完全不错。

496
00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:23.950
But I noticed that there are a few episodes where Michael has several misused words, like three or more.
但我注意到有几集迈克尔用错了好几个词，比如三个或更多。

497
00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:31.630
And those episodes were The Convention, Dinner Party, Job Fair, and New Boss.
这些剧集包括《大会》、《晚宴》、《招聘会》和《新老板》。

498
00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:35.030
Guess what all of those episodes have in common?
你猜这些剧集有什么共同点？

499
00:23:35.270 --> 00:23:36.310
The same writer.
同一个编剧。

500
00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:39.070
Gene Stepnitzky and Lee Eisenberg.
吉恩·斯蒂普尼茨基和李·艾森伯格。

501
00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:39.630
Huh.
嗯。

502
00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:41.770
So I reached out to them.
所以我联系了他们。

503
00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.030
And I was like, guys, what do I do with this?
我就问，伙计们，这个我该怎么处理？

504
00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:47.850
Are you guys the mangled word guys?
你们是负责那些“乱用词”的吗？

505
00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:48.370
Yeah.
是的。

506
00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:50.610
Like Brent Forrester is the pun guy.
就像布伦特·福雷斯特是负责双关语的。

507
00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:51.750
He loves the puns.
他超爱双关语。

508
00:23:51.770 --> 00:23:52.050
Yes.
没错。

509
00:23:52.210 --> 00:23:54.230
Aaron Schur was our cold open fella.
亚伦·舒尔是我们负责开场戏的家伙。

510
00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:54.590
Right?
对吧？

511
00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:55.010
Right.
对。

512
00:23:55.170 --> 00:23:57.490
So tell me, were you the mangled word guys?
所以告诉我，你们是负责乱用词的人吗？

513
00:23:57.670 --> 00:23:58.570
And they said no.
他们说不是。

514
00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:00.490
They said it was no single writer.
他们说这并非出自某一位编剧之手。

515
00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:05.530
And they said it was a combination of written lines and Steve improvisations.
他们说这是剧本台词和史蒂夫即兴发挥的结合。

516
00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:09.250
Then they told me the ones that Steve improvised in their episodes.
然后他们告诉了我史蒂夫在他们剧集中即兴发挥的那些词。

517
00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.510
So they said Prodigal Son Returns from the convention was a Steve improv.
他们说《浪子回头》那集里的“convention”是史蒂夫即兴说的。

518
00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:19.530
Make Yourself to Home from Dinner Party was an improv.
《晚宴》那集里的“Make Yourself to Home”也是即兴的。

519
00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:24.710
And Okie After Birth was a Steve improv from Dinner Party.
还有《晚宴》里的“Okie After Birth”也是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

520
00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:33.350
And then they said that their personal favorite mangled word, escape goat, from Product Recall, was written by Justin Spitzer.
然后他们说他们个人最喜欢的乱用词，出自《产品召回》的“escape goat”，是贾斯汀·斯皮策写的。

521
00:24:34.350 --> 00:24:36.930
I just love the system that we had in the office.
我真的很喜欢我们在办公室里的那种工作模式。

522
00:24:36.930 --> 00:24:44.690
I feel like our system of including the actors in the creation of their characters, trusting us to improvise,
我觉得我们让演员参与角色创作，信任我们去即兴发挥的模式，

523
00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:51.090
it just led to this amazing character trait of Michael Scott that we all love.
造就了迈克尔·斯科特这个我们都深爱的绝妙角色特质。

524
00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:51.390
Yeah.
没错。

525
00:24:52.530 --> 00:25:02.090
And lady, if I could give you a dundee right now, I would give you a dundee for being the Michael Scott of office ladies for your mangled words.
这位女士，如果我现在能给你颁发一个邓迪奖，我会因为你在“办公室女士”里那些乱用的词，给你颁发一个迈克尔·斯科特式的邓迪奖。

526
00:25:02.390 --> 00:25:08.550
Me, Sam, and Cassie, we traded some text messages trying to remember all of the words you've mangled.
我和萨姆还有卡西发了些短信，试图回忆起你所有乱用过的词。

527
00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:13.450
So, Angela, I shared my favorite, and it is Kid in a Candy Jar.
安吉拉，我分享了我最喜欢的一个，就是“Kid in a Candy Jar”。

528
00:25:13.670 --> 00:25:14.570
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

529
00:25:14.570 --> 00:25:15.590
That's a classic.
那是经典。

530
00:25:15.770 --> 00:25:16.410
I love it.
我超爱那个。

531
00:25:16.470 --> 00:25:17.290
Classic Kinsey right there.
典型的金西风格。

532
00:25:17.290 --> 00:25:19.290
The kids inside that candy jar.
糖果罐里的孩子。

533
00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:19.630
Yeah.
是啊。

534
00:25:19.950 --> 00:25:20.210
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

535
00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:20.910
That's me.
那就是我。

536
00:25:22.090 --> 00:25:23.530
God, that brings me back.
天哪，那让我想起过去。

537
00:25:24.910 --> 00:25:32.050
The one I immediately thought of because I got it from you in a postcard on a frame is Peep Shot.
我立刻想到的是“Peep Shot”，因为我是在你寄给我的明信片相框上看到的。

538
00:25:32.390 --> 00:25:35.150
Peep Shot instead of Spy Shot.
把“Spy Shot”说成了“Peep Shot”。

539
00:25:35.330 --> 00:25:35.670
Yeah.
没错。

540
00:25:36.690 --> 00:25:38.590
And Life Intimidating Art.
还有“Life Intimidating Art”。

541
00:25:39.930 --> 00:25:40.530
Yes.
是的。

542
00:25:40.910 --> 00:25:42.630
Those are our favorites, Ange.
那些是我们的最爱，安吉。

543
00:25:42.930 --> 00:25:43.370
Life Intimidating Art.
“Life Intimidating Art”。

544
00:25:43.470 --> 00:25:44.750
It might be my favorite.
那可能是我最喜欢的。

545
00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:46.230
The Kid in a Candy Jar.
“Kid in a Candy Jar”。

546
00:25:46.310 --> 00:25:47.810
I think about that once a week.
我每周都会想起它一次。

547
00:25:48.810 --> 00:25:50.730
That lives in your mind.
它一直萦绕在你的脑海里。

548
00:25:51.310 --> 00:25:54.270
Well, you know, I just spent a week with my mom.
嗯，你知道，我刚和妈妈待了一周。

549
00:25:54.390 --> 00:25:55.210
It was so wonderful.
真是太美好了。

550
00:25:55.550 --> 00:25:58.210
And I just come by this so honeSt.
我这毛病真是天生的。

551
00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:02.410
So, I wear it like a badge of honor because my mom said, are you on Twitter?
所以我把它当成一种荣誉勋章，因为我妈问我，你在用推特吗？

552
00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:06.610
I was like, no, I'm not on Twitter.
我说，没有，我没用推特。

553
00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:07.290
Really, Mom?
真的吗，妈？

554
00:26:07.450 --> 00:26:08.030
Not really.
其实并不是。

555
00:26:10.910 --> 00:26:16.150
Well, maybe this is why I love this quality so much in Michael Scott is because I love it in you.
嗯，也许这就是为什么我这么喜欢迈克尔·斯科特身上的这种特质，因为我也在你身上看到了这种特质。

556
00:26:16.430 --> 00:26:16.790
Yes.
是的。

557
00:26:19.710 --> 00:26:21.970
I really enjoyed that so much.
我真的很喜欢这一点。

558
00:26:22.150 --> 00:26:27.710
You know, one of the things I loved most about Michael Scott is how much he hates technology.
你知道，关于迈克尔·斯科特，我最喜欢的一点就是他有多讨厌科技。

559
00:26:28.390 --> 00:26:29.790
I hate technology.
我讨厌科技。

560
00:26:30.150 --> 00:26:39.190
You know, I don't want, gosh, I don't want to go through emails and I hate it when I have to update my phone or if we get a new remote for the TV, it just pisses me off.
你知道，我不想，天哪，我不想去处理电子邮件，而且我讨厌更新手机，或者换个新的电视遥控器，这简直让我火大。

561
00:26:39.370 --> 00:26:41.610
I just want my damn old technology.
我只想用我那该死的老式设备。

562
00:26:41.650 --> 00:26:43.670
I'd be so happy with a flip phone.
如果能用翻盖手机，我会非常开心的。

563
00:26:43.790 --> 00:26:44.530
I really would.
真的会。

564
00:26:44.690 --> 00:26:45.330
It's true.
这是真的。

565
00:26:45.330 --> 00:26:48.390
And I feel like Michael and I have this in common.
我觉得我和迈克尔在这点上很像。

566
00:26:48.670 --> 00:26:56.110
And like you, Jenna, I found some amazing compilations that people have put together called Michael vs. Technology.
而且像你一样，珍娜，我发现了一些人们制作的精彩合集，叫作“迈克尔大战科技”。

567
00:26:57.610 --> 00:27:00.510
But the clip was so long, I'm just going to share a few.
但那个片段太长了，我只分享其中几个。

568
00:27:00.730 --> 00:27:04.210
He hates technology so much every single season.
每一季里他都那么讨厌科技。

569
00:27:04.450 --> 00:27:10.330
Well, I don't know what you're going to share, but I love when he lies about having a PowerPoint presentation ready.
好吧，我不知道你要分享什么，但我最喜欢他撒谎说自己准备好了PPT演示文稿的时候。

570
00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:11.610
Well, that's one of them.
嗯，那确实是其中之一。

571
00:27:12.390 --> 00:27:19.470
But before I get into all that, I have a fan question from a Joshua Snyder in Los Angeles, California.
但在进入正题之前，我有一个来自加利福尼亚州洛杉矶的粉丝约书亚·斯奈德的问题。

572
00:27:20.190 --> 00:27:20.930
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

573
00:27:21.210 --> 00:27:24.550
I know a Joshua Snyder in Los Angeles.
我认识一个在洛杉矶的约书亚·斯奈德。

574
00:27:24.950 --> 00:27:26.170
What is his question?
他的问题是什么？

575
00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:27.170
So do I.
我也认识。

576
00:27:28.010 --> 00:27:32.030
I told him I was doing Michael vs. Technology, and he was very intrigued.
我告诉他我要做“迈克尔大战科技”这个主题，他非常感兴趣。

577
00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:37.130
He said, ladies, I have wondered what Michael Scott would do with chat GPT.
他说，女士们，我一直很好奇迈克尔·斯科特会怎么用ChatGPT。

578
00:27:37.350 --> 00:27:38.270
Oh, my goodness.
哦，天哪。

579
00:27:38.590 --> 00:27:39.030
I know.
我知道。

580
00:27:39.490 --> 00:27:45.350
Josh said, so I asked it what the character Michael Scott would use it for, and here's what it had to say.
乔什说，所以我问了它迈克尔·斯科特这个角色会用它来做什么，以下是它的回答。

581
00:27:45.530 --> 00:27:45.650
No.
不会吧。

582
00:27:47.070 --> 00:27:47.550
Yes.
是的。

583
00:27:47.910 --> 00:27:49.250
What did it say?
它说了什么？

584
00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:50.290
Josh, look what he did.
乔什，看他做了什么。

585
00:27:50.350 --> 00:27:51.690
He did a document and everything.
他甚至还做了一个文档。

586
00:27:52.210 --> 00:27:54.230
What would Michael Scott do with AI?
迈克尔·斯科特会用人工智能做什么？

587
00:27:54.230 --> 00:27:58.070
This is what AI says Michael Scott would do with AI.
这就是人工智能认为迈克尔·斯科特会用人工智能做的事。

588
00:27:58.410 --> 00:28:00.870
This is very, very, very funny to me.
这对我来说真的、真的、真的太搞笑了。

589
00:28:01.210 --> 00:28:02.730
These are the top 10 things.
这是前十名。

590
00:28:02.850 --> 00:28:02.990
Ready?
准备好了吗？

591
00:28:03.910 --> 00:28:07.830
Number one, Michael would ask ridiculous questions.
第一名，迈克尔会问一些荒谬的问题。

592
00:28:08.130 --> 00:28:08.570
True.
没错。

593
00:28:09.550 --> 00:28:12.390
Like, what is the world's best office prank, for example?
比如，什么是世界上最好的办公室恶作剧？

594
00:28:12.770 --> 00:28:12.990
Okay.
好的。

595
00:28:13.510 --> 00:28:16.010
Number two, Michael would write movie scripts.
第二名，迈克尔会写电影剧本。

596
00:28:16.790 --> 00:28:17.390
Yes.
是的。

597
00:28:17.990 --> 00:28:20.150
Perhaps a Michael Scarn the prequel.
也许是《迈克尔·斯卡恩》的前传。

598
00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:22.890
This is what AI said?
这是人工智能说的？

599
00:28:23.050 --> 00:28:23.270
Yes.
是的。

600
00:28:23.270 --> 00:28:25.650
How does AI know Michael Scott so well?
人工智能怎么会这么了解迈克尔·斯科特？

601
00:28:25.710 --> 00:28:26.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

602
00:28:27.010 --> 00:28:34.070
It also says his scripts would spend hours detailing extravagant and nonsensical plot twists that always end with him as the hero.
上面还说他的剧本会花上几小时去详述那些离谱又荒唐的情节反转，而且结局总是让他当英雄。

603
00:28:34.470 --> 00:28:34.970
Wow.
哇。

604
00:28:35.510 --> 00:28:39.130
Number three, Michael would use it to plan office parties.
第三点，迈克尔会用它来策划办公室派对。

605
00:28:39.790 --> 00:28:42.870
They would be fun, but also professional, but mostly fun.
