今天我们要聊聊PowerPoint。

766
00:36:10.940 --> 00:36:11.460
PowerPoint.
PowerPoint。

767
00:36:11.880 --> 00:36:12.220
PowerPoint.
PowerPoint。

768
00:36:12.760 --> 00:36:13.020
PowerPoint.
PowerPoint。

769
00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:16.120
Yes, I forgot about Ryan's presentation.
没错，我忘了瑞安的演示文稿了。

770
00:36:16.120 --> 00:36:20.900
And yes, it would have been nice to do well with the first presentation that he had given me.
而且确实，如果他交给我的第一份演示文稿能做得好一点就好了。

771
00:36:20.900 --> 00:36:23.080
But you know what else would have been nice?
但你知道还有什么更好吗？

772
00:36:23.620 --> 00:36:24.820
Winning the lottery.
中彩票。

773
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:29.460
And the best way to start is to hit start.
最好的开始方式就是点击开始。

774
00:36:30.300 --> 00:36:33.080
And up comes the toolbar.
然后工具栏就出来了。

775
00:36:33.720 --> 00:36:34.840
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

776
00:36:34.840 --> 00:36:39.100
What we have to do here is go to run.
我们要做的就是点击运行。

777
00:36:39.520 --> 00:36:45.580
And then you look up to PowerPoint.
然后你找到PowerPoint。

778
00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:48.860
And we are in.
我们就进去了。

779
00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:50.460
And we are going to register.
我们要注册一下。

780
00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.260
You hit register.
点击注册。

781
00:36:53.280 --> 00:36:54.000
Updates are ready.
更新已就绪。

782
00:36:54.180 --> 00:36:55.060
I should update.
我应该更新一下。

783
00:36:56.580 --> 00:36:56.980
Um.
嗯。

784
00:36:58.440 --> 00:36:59.540
Estimated time, 12 minutes.
预计时间，12分钟。

785
00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:01.180
So this should take about 5 or 10 minutes.
所以这大概需要5到10分钟。

786
00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:03.240
This is the first time you've opened PowerPoint.
这是你第一次打开PowerPoint吧。

787
00:37:03.960 --> 00:37:04.360
Why?
为什么？

788
00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:07.080
You didn't prepare a presentation at all, did you?
你根本没准备演示文稿，对吧？

789
00:37:07.160 --> 00:37:07.400
You know what?
你知道吗？

790
00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:08.940
I had a really rough night.
我昨晚过得很糟糕。

791
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:15.960
You know what's so funny is just now playing that, the part where you laughed is the same part where you break in the scene.
你知道最搞笑的是，刚才播放的时候，你笑的那部分正好就是你当时笑场的那部分。

792
00:37:16.180 --> 00:37:16.720
Oh, really?
噢，真的吗？

793
00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:17.320
Yes.
是的。

794
00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:20.320
The part where it's like now you have to register.
就是那句“现在你必须注册”的时候。

795
00:37:22.760 --> 00:37:23.920
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

796
00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:25.600
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

797
00:37:26.040 --> 00:37:30.540
So I am curious why you laughed both times in the same place.
所以我很好奇为什么你两次都在同一个地方笑了。

798
00:37:30.740 --> 00:37:32.480
Once, what, 15 years ago?
一次是，什么，15年前？

799
00:37:32.660 --> 00:37:33.100
Yeah.
没错。

800
00:37:33.100 --> 00:37:37.980
And once today, what is it about the fact that he had to then go register?
还有一次是今天，他必须去注册这件事到底有什么好笑的？

801
00:37:38.200 --> 00:37:39.200
What is that?
那是什么？

802
00:37:39.320 --> 00:37:42.480
Because it became so obvious he had never opened it.
因为很明显他从来没打开过它。

803
00:37:42.880 --> 00:37:45.060
Like, that was the giveaway.
就像，那是个破绽。

804
00:37:45.440 --> 00:37:54.380
Like, up until that point, you could maybe believe that he thought his job was to walk you through it from the very beginning.
就像，在那之前，你可能还会相信他以为自己的工作是从头到尾带我们过一遍。

805
00:37:54.680 --> 00:37:54.900
Right.
没错。

806
00:37:54.900 --> 00:37:57.300
And that we're a room full of idiots.
而且以为我们是一屋子的白痴。

807
00:37:57.660 --> 00:38:01.700
And so that's how he's giving this PowerPoint presentation.
所以他才那样做PPT演示。

808
00:38:02.360 --> 00:38:08.180
But when it's clear he never registered, you know he has put no effort into it.
但当很明显他根本没注册过时，你就知道他根本没下功夫。

809
00:38:08.280 --> 00:38:11.780
I mean, we all knew that he was just tap dancing his way through this anyway.
我是说，我们都知道他反正只是在敷衍了事。

810
00:38:11.940 --> 00:38:12.140
Right.
没错。

811
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:14.080
That is the moment where he's caught.
那一刻他被抓包了。

812
00:38:14.380 --> 00:38:14.620
Yeah.
是啊。

813
00:38:14.920 --> 00:38:15.560
That's funny.
真好笑。

814
00:38:15.560 --> 00:38:16.240
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

815
00:38:16.340 --> 00:38:17.420
I think I loved that.
我想我喜欢那个。

816
00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:18.040
I did, too.
我也喜欢。

817
00:38:18.180 --> 00:38:22.480
I also loved when he said, okay, now it's just going to take 12 minutes.
我也很喜欢他说，好了，现在只需要12分钟。

818
00:38:23.380 --> 00:38:23.820
Yeah.
是啊。

819
00:38:25.640 --> 00:38:32.500
I was the PowerPoint expert in my office when I was an administrative assistant in St. Louis, Missouri.
我在密苏里州圣路易斯当行政助理时，是办公室里的PPT专家。

820
00:38:32.600 --> 00:38:38.040
I would make the PowerPoint presentations for all of the salespeople, for the wholesale staff.
我会为所有的销售人员，为批发部门制作PPT演示文稿。

821
00:38:38.040 --> 00:38:47.700
If they had to go off and meet with a client, they gave me the information they wanted, and I put it into a PowerPoint for them, and I taught them how to use it.
如果他们要出去见客户，他们会把想要的信息给我，我帮他们做成PPT，还会教他们怎么用。

822
00:38:48.320 --> 00:38:52.260
That is maybe my favorite thing that I have heard this whole month.
这可能是我这个月听到的最让我喜欢的事情了。

823
00:38:52.260 --> 00:38:55.380
You labeled yourself the PowerPoint expert.
你自封为PPT专家。

824
00:38:55.740 --> 00:39:06.720
I was of that office, and I was the youngest person in the office, and I think today how, Angela, we run into this all the time trying to post on Instagram,
我是那个办公室里最年轻的人，我今天还在想，安吉拉，我们经常遇到这种情况，就像尝试在Instagram上发帖时，

825
00:39:06.720 --> 00:39:11.440
and I don't know how to get the ratio and then the tagging and the this.
我不知道怎么调整比例，还有标记什么的。

826
00:39:11.540 --> 00:39:12.860
It's very high effort for me.
对我来说这太费劲了。

827
00:39:13.360 --> 00:39:18.700
And then we had this babysitter over, this young gal, and she was like, oh, didn't you know you can just blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah?
然后我们请了个保姆，那个年轻姑娘说，噢，你不知道你可以直接这样那样那样吗？

828
00:39:18.700 --> 00:39:20.460
And I'm like, oh, no, I did not.
我就说，噢，不，我不知道。

829
00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:22.380
No, I did not know that.
不，我确实不知道。

830
00:39:22.540 --> 00:39:26.180
So I feel like that's who I was to those people in the office.
所以我感觉我当时对办公室里的那些人来说就是那样。

831
00:39:26.180 --> 00:39:32.300
I was this young'un who just immediately knew how to use PowerPoint, and they were always so clunky with it.
我是那个立刻就知道怎么用PPT的年轻人，而他们总是用得很笨拙。

832
00:39:32.360 --> 00:39:33.000
You were Ryan.
你就是瑞安。

833
00:39:33.820 --> 00:39:35.120
I guess I was.
我想我是。

834
00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:37.280
I'm Michael Scott, and you're Ryan.
我是迈克尔·斯科特，你是瑞安。

835
00:39:39.100 --> 00:39:45.720
Well, listen, why don't we take a break, and when we come back, I did a deep dive into Michael's family of origin.
好吧，听着，我们休息一下，回来后，我会深入挖掘迈克尔的原生家庭。

836
00:39:46.400 --> 00:39:47.560
Ooh, I can't wait.
噢，我等不及了。

837
00:39:47.840 --> 00:40:08.500
We are back, and before the break, we discussed everything we do know about Michael Scott, but there is one very big thing that we do not know much about,
我们回来了，休息之前，我们讨论了关于迈克尔·斯科特我们所知道的一切，但有一件非常重要的事情我们了解不多，

838
00:40:08.580 --> 00:40:10.200
and that is his family of origin.
那就是他的原生家庭。

839
00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:14.860
And we got a ton of questions about Michael and his backstory.
我们收到了大量关于迈克尔和他背景故事的问题。

840
00:40:15.120 --> 00:40:18.720
This was our fan mail flurry when we asked people to write us about Michael Scott.
这是我们要求大家写信给我们谈论迈克尔·斯科特时收到的粉丝邮件狂潮。

841
00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:20.820
Here is just a sampling.
这里只是其中一部分。

842
00:40:21.180 --> 00:40:23.020
This one from Victoria L.
这封来自维多利亚·L。

843
00:40:23.180 --> 00:40:25.060
in Hollis, New Hampshire, who said,
在新罕布什尔州霍利斯，她说，

844
00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:29.400
I always wanted to know more about the relationship between Michael and his mother.
我一直想了解更多关于迈克尔和他母亲之间的关系。

845
00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:35.100
I so wish that we could have seen at least one episode with them interacting that wasn't just a phone call.
我真希望我们至少能看到一集他们互动的戏份，而不是只有电话通话。

846
00:40:35.380 --> 00:40:38.680
I have always wondered why there wasn't more of this relationship.
我一直很纳闷为什么没有更多关于这种关系的描写。

847
00:40:39.260 --> 00:40:43.200
Was there ever a storyline pitched where we met Michael's mom?
有没有过关于我们见到迈克尔妈妈的剧情构思？

848
00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:46.400
Well, Victoria, you are correct.
嗯，维多利亚，你说得对。

849
00:40:46.400 --> 00:40:48.760
We do not ever meet Michael's mom.
我们确实从未见过迈克尔的妈妈。

850
00:40:48.780 --> 00:40:50.960
I don't even think we learned her name.
我觉得我们甚至连她的名字都不知道。

851
00:40:51.180 --> 00:40:54.220
I looked everywhere, and I never found her name.
我到处都找遍了，但从来没找到她的名字。

852
00:40:54.600 --> 00:40:58.520
The first time we hear from her is in season two, the injury.
我们第一次听到关于她的消息是在第二季的《受伤》那一集。

853
00:40:58.760 --> 00:41:01.960
Michael calls her on the phone, and we hear her voice.
迈克尔给她打了电话，我们听到了她的声音。

854
00:41:02.220 --> 00:41:04.380
She was played by June Squibb.
她是由琼·斯奎布饰演的。

855
00:41:04.920 --> 00:41:09.020
We also got the impression that Pam and Michael's mom talk quite often.
我们还感觉到帕姆和迈克尔的妈妈经常聊天。

856
00:41:09.740 --> 00:41:14.040
Then in season four, Michael calls his mom from the nightclub in Night Out.
然后在第四季，迈克尔在《夜生活》那一集中从夜店给妈妈打了电话。

857
00:41:14.260 --> 00:41:18.560
And in season five, he calls and tells her he's engaged to Holly.
在第五季，他打电话告诉她自己和霍莉订婚了。

858
00:41:18.740 --> 00:41:19.900
He's not engaged to Holly.
他其实并没有和霍莉订婚。

859
00:41:20.180 --> 00:41:22.320
This was a thing he was doing with his mom.
这是他和他妈妈之间玩的一个梗。

860
00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:28.280
And then in Michael Scott Paper Company, he calls her again and says that Ryan and Pam are annoying him.
后来在《迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司》那一集，他又打电话给她，说瑞安和帕姆让他很烦。

861
00:41:28.280 --> 00:41:31.280
So we set up that he calls his mom pretty often.
所以我们设定他经常给妈妈打电话。

862
00:41:31.680 --> 00:41:38.980
And while we never ended up meeting her, there was a very famous person who lobbied very hard to play Michael's mom.
虽然我们最终没能让她出场，但有一位非常著名的人物曾极力争取饰演迈克尔的妈妈。

863
00:41:39.220 --> 00:41:43.000
And you're going to be so incredibly bummed when I tell you who it is.
当我告诉你她是谁时，你一定会感到无比遗憾。

864
00:41:43.160 --> 00:41:44.360
You love this person.
你很喜欢这个人。

865
00:41:44.700 --> 00:41:46.360
Wait, let me get this straight.
等等，让我理一理。

866
00:41:46.700 --> 00:41:51.860
There was an actor who would reach out and say, please, can I play Michael's mom?
有一位演员主动联系剧组说，求求你们，我能演迈克尔的妈妈吗？

867
00:41:51.980 --> 00:41:52.620
Please, please, please.
求求你们，求求你们，求求你们。

868
00:41:52.860 --> 00:41:54.960
Over and over and over again.
一遍又一遍地请求。

869
00:41:55.180 --> 00:41:57.340
And they were like, nah, we're good?
而剧组却说，不用了，我们不需要？

870
00:41:57.340 --> 00:42:02.380
They were like, you're too famous, and we don't cast famous people on our show.
他们说，你太出名了，我们剧组不请大明星。

871
00:42:02.400 --> 00:42:03.480
Is it Carol Burnett?
是卡罗尔·伯内特吗？

872
00:42:03.600 --> 00:42:04.540
It's Carol Burnett.
就是卡罗尔·伯内特。

873
00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:05.200
Get out!
别开玩笑了！

874
00:42:05.840 --> 00:42:06.860
Carol Burnett.
卡罗尔·伯内特。

875
00:42:07.720 --> 00:42:08.180
Ugh!
啊！

876
00:42:09.260 --> 00:42:09.900
Yeah.
没错。

877
00:42:10.380 --> 00:42:15.140
And Greg said if we ever did see Michael's mom, she had the role.
格雷格说，如果我们真的要让迈克尔的妈妈出场，这个角色就是她的。

878
00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:21.220
But in early seasons, he was hesitant to cast her because she was so famous.
但在早期几季，他很犹豫要不要选她，因为她太出名了。

879
00:42:21.220 --> 00:42:28.220
By the way, we don't hear anything about Michael's mom in, like, seasons six and seven when we had broken our rule.
顺便说一下，在第六季和第七季我们打破了不请大明星的规矩后，就再也没听到关于迈克尔妈妈的消息了。

880
00:42:28.700 --> 00:42:36.500
But she has given several interviews where she said, I keep calling them, but they keep changing their number.
但她曾在几次采访中说，我一直在给他们打电话，但他们一直在换号码。

881
00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:37.400
I don't know.
我不知道。

882
00:42:38.940 --> 00:42:42.560
And this was confirmed on our season four DVD commentators.
这一点在我们的第四季DVD评论音轨中得到了证实。

883
00:42:42.700 --> 00:42:47.120
The writers said that if we ever meet Michael's mom, Carol Burnett would play her.
编剧们说，如果我们真的要让迈克尔的妈妈出场，卡罗尔·伯内特会出演这个角色。

884
00:42:47.360 --> 00:42:48.840
She has volunteered for the role.
她曾主动请缨出演这个角色。

885
00:42:49.240 --> 00:42:50.560
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

886
00:42:50.820 --> 00:42:51.340
I know.
我知道。

887
00:42:51.680 --> 00:42:52.680
Carol Burnett.
卡罗尔·伯内特。

888
00:42:52.960 --> 00:42:53.400
I know.
我知道。

889
00:42:53.840 --> 00:42:54.340
Yeah.
没错。

890
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:58.980
Maybe she could play one of our moms on Mom Detectives.
也许她可以演我们《妈妈侦探》里的其中一位妈妈。

891
00:42:59.580 --> 00:43:00.100
Yes.
对。

892
00:43:01.640 --> 00:43:03.640
Maybe not the role she was looking for.
可能不是她想要的那种角色。

893
00:43:03.700 --> 00:43:04.240
Probably not.
大概不是。

894
00:43:04.240 --> 00:43:06.180
She might be like, ladies, I'm good.
她可能会说，女士们，我还是算了吧。

895
00:43:08.440 --> 00:43:09.120
All right.
好吧。

896
00:43:09.240 --> 00:43:11.480
Well, that's your tidbit about Michael's mom.
这就是关于迈克尔妈妈的小花絮。

897
00:43:11.780 --> 00:43:14.460
We also got a fan question from Stephanie M.
我们还收到了一位来自爱荷华州的粉丝斯蒂芬妮·M的提问。

898
00:43:14.520 --> 00:43:17.400
in Iowa who said, what's the story with Michael's dad?
她问，迈克尔的爸爸是怎么回事？

899
00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:24.900
We hear about his mom, his stepdad Jeff, and even his step-half sister, his nephew, but I don't remember him ever talking about his dad.
我们听过他妈妈、继父杰夫，甚至是他同母异父的妹妹和侄子的事，但我记得他从没提过他爸爸。

900
00:43:25.140 --> 00:43:26.480
Is that ever addressed?
这事儿有交代过吗？

901
00:43:27.120 --> 00:43:30.240
Was there ever a backstory to Michael?
迈克尔有过背景故事吗？

902
00:43:30.360 --> 00:43:31.600
Was this discussed?
讨论过这件事吗？

903
00:43:32.840 --> 00:43:40.900
Well, I traded messages with Greg Daniels who said, I know, how many texts did he get from us for this episode?
嗯，我和格雷格·丹尼尔斯互发了消息，他说，我知道，为了这一集我们给他发了多少条短信？

904
00:43:41.080 --> 00:43:41.840
Too many.
太多了。

905
00:43:42.200 --> 00:43:42.980
So many.
多得数不清。

906
00:43:43.360 --> 00:43:50.180
He said for a very long time there was a card on the wall that said Michael reunites with dad.
他说在很长一段时间里，墙上都贴着一张卡片，上面写着迈克尔与父亲重逢。

907
00:43:50.740 --> 00:43:53.280
Oh, we just never got to it.
哦，我们只是没能拍出来。

908
00:43:53.920 --> 00:43:54.300
Yeah.
是啊。

909
00:43:54.480 --> 00:43:57.980
Greg said that we almost met Michael's dad in season seven.
格雷格说我们在第七季差点就见到迈克尔的父亲了。

910
00:43:58.300 --> 00:44:00.920
That is the season where we met his nephew.
那一季我们见到了他的侄子。

911
00:44:01.380 --> 00:44:04.700
You know, that's when he spanks his nephew in nepotism.
你知道，就是他在《任人唯亲》那一集里打他侄子屁股的时候。

912
00:44:04.860 --> 00:44:05.040
Yeah.
没错。

913
00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:07.640
And then he has to go to counseling with Toby.
然后他不得不和托比一起去接受心理咨询。

914
00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:19.380
Well, some of the early concepts for that episode were that Toby would draw out this really personal information from Michael about his family of origin, particularly his dad.
嗯，那一集早期的一些构思是，托比会从迈克尔那里引出关于他原生家庭，特别是他父亲的非常私人的信息。

915
00:44:19.380 --> 00:44:30.020
We were going to find out that Michael only saw his dad three times a year growing up, and Toby was going to reunite Michael and his dad.
我们本来打算揭露迈克尔在成长过程中一年只见过他父亲三次，而托比打算让迈克尔和他的父亲重聚。

916
00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:31.560
The dad would come into the office.
他父亲会来到办公室。

917
00:44:31.560 --> 00:44:32.920
It would be a surprise.
那会是一个惊喜。

918
00:44:33.500 --> 00:44:35.220
But they ended up changing it.
但他们最终改变了主意。

919
00:44:35.420 --> 00:44:36.120
It never happened.
这事儿没发生。

920
00:44:36.660 --> 00:44:42.860
And we never even got so far as to, like, put out a casting notice for the role or anything.
我们甚至都没走到发布选角通知之类的地步。

921
00:44:42.860 --> 00:44:44.080
They just pivoted.
他们只是转换了方向。

922
00:44:44.840 --> 00:44:48.680
But that is the closest we got to meeting Michael's dad.
但那确实是我们最接近见到迈克尔父亲的一次。

923
00:44:49.040 --> 00:44:59.560
And then finally, in my deep dive on Michael's family of origin, I did find one moment, a story from his childhood that we shot, and it was deleted.
最后，在我深入挖掘迈克尔原生家庭的过程中，我确实发现了一个瞬间，一个我们拍摄过但后来被删掉的童年故事。

924
00:45:00.240 --> 00:45:02.480
It's a deleted scene from The Surplus.
那是《剩余物资》里的一段删减片段。

925
00:45:02.880 --> 00:45:07.460
This is part of the Peacock Superfan episode, but I thought it would be fun to listen.
这是Peacock超级粉丝版剧集的一部分，但我觉得听听会很有趣。

926
00:45:09.040 --> 00:45:11.880
I would like to tell you a little story.
我想给你们讲个小故事。

927
00:45:12.860 --> 00:45:14.100
Let me call you right back.
我马上回给你。

928
00:45:14.280 --> 00:45:14.660
Okay.
好的。

929
00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:17.460
About a boy named...
关于一个叫……的男孩。

930
00:45:18.200 --> 00:45:19.440
That doesn't even matter.
那根本不重要。

931
00:45:19.600 --> 00:45:20.440
Could be any one of you.
可能是你们中的任何一个。

932
00:45:21.260 --> 00:45:26.920
And like any other 12-year-old boy, he wanted a pippy long-stocking doll for Christmas.
像其他任何12岁的男孩一样，他圣诞节想要一个长袜子皮皮玩偶。

933
00:45:28.580 --> 00:45:31.300
But his evil stepfather, Jeff, said,
但他邪恶的继父杰夫说：

934
00:45:31.500 --> 00:45:33.360
No, you may not have what you want.
不，你不能要你想要的。

935
00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.140
You must have a football.
你必须得要一个橄榄球。

936
00:45:36.060 --> 00:45:42.680
And the boy cried, and he cried, and he cried, and he held his breath as long as he could, and he wouldn't eat his dinner.
那个男孩哭了，哭啊哭，他尽可能久地屏住呼吸，而且他不肯吃晚饭。

937
00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:44.420
But you know something?
但你们知道吗？

938
00:45:45.200 --> 00:45:50.420
It turns out that Jeff was right, because I already had a G.I.
事实证明杰夫是对的，因为我已经有了特种部队玩偶、

939
00:45:50.520 --> 00:45:58.040
Joe, and a Stretch Armstrong, and a Malibu Barbie, and a Major Matt Mason, which technically is enough for a tea party.
伸缩超人、马里布芭比，还有马特·梅森少校，从技术上讲，这些足够办一场茶会了。

940
00:45:58.320 --> 00:45:59.500
So my point is this.
所以我的意思是。

941
00:45:59.700 --> 00:46:02.460
I didn't need what I thought I needed.
我并不需要我以为我需要的东西。

942
00:46:02.780 --> 00:46:07.960
What I needed was to learn how to appreciate what I had.
我需要的是学会如何欣赏我已经拥有的东西。

943
00:46:08.080 --> 00:46:10.220
Which in this case was enough dolls to have tea with.
在这种情况下，就是足够用来喝下午茶的玩偶。

944
00:46:10.460 --> 00:46:10.900
Exactly.
没错。

945
00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:13.120
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

946
00:46:13.300 --> 00:46:17.020
A little sad insight into his childhood.
对他童年的一点点悲伤洞察。

947
00:46:17.380 --> 00:46:19.020
Jeff is such a dick.
杰夫真是个混蛋。

948
00:46:19.280 --> 00:46:19.960
I know.
我知道。

949
00:46:19.960 --> 00:46:20.800
I know.
我知道。

950
00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:30.160
And, you know, people were very curious if it was like a decision to keep his backstory kind of vague.
而且，你知道，人们很好奇这是否是一种让他的背景故事保持模糊的决定。

951
00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:32.500
But Greg said it was not.
但格雷格说事实并非如此。

952
00:46:32.780 --> 00:46:37.340
He said they pitched a lot of different stories, but they just never really took root.
他说他们提出了很多不同的故事构思，但都没能真正扎根。

953
00:46:37.340 --> 00:46:42.720
But after they introduced the idea of the stepdad, Jeff, that happens in season three,
但在他们引入继父杰夫这个角色后，也就是第三季发生的事，

954
00:46:43.080 --> 00:46:50.300
it sort of became part of Michael's backstory that he was basically raised by Jeff and his mom.
迈克尔基本上是由杰夫和他妈妈抚养长大的，这在某种程度上成了迈克尔背景故事的一部分。

955
00:46:50.540 --> 00:46:50.660
Yeah.
是啊。

956
00:46:50.660 --> 00:46:55.360
And so sometimes you got speeches like the one in the surplus.
所以有时你会听到像“盈余”那一集里的演讲。

957
00:46:55.740 --> 00:46:56.020
Right.
没错。

958
00:46:56.300 --> 00:46:58.360
But there wasn't much more than what we saw.
但除了我们看到的那些，并没有更多内容了。

959
00:46:58.500 --> 00:47:02.120
There was not some, like, big decision they were holding back or anything like that.
并没有什么他们刻意隐瞒的重大决定之类的东西。

960
00:47:02.780 --> 00:47:05.560
Well, everyone, we got so many questions on that topic.
好了，各位，我们收到了很多关于这个话题的问题。

961
00:47:05.560 --> 00:47:07.980
I really tried to deep dive that for you.
我真的试着为你们深入挖掘了一下。

962
00:47:07.980 --> 00:47:12.380
So I hope that was a little bit satisfying that we got a little more information about that.
所以我希望我们能提供更多相关信息，让大家感到一点满足。

963
00:47:12.940 --> 00:47:13.200
Yeah.
是啊。

964
00:47:13.380 --> 00:47:16.820
I mean, it still paints a pretty bleak picture for Michael growing up.
我的意思是，这对于迈克尔的成长经历来说，依然描绘了一幅相当凄凉的画面。

965
00:47:17.180 --> 00:47:17.500
Yeah.
是啊。

966
00:47:18.720 --> 00:47:25.120
Well, you know, since this is all things Michael Scott, we got a fan question that I was really curious about as well.
嗯，你知道，既然这期节目全是关于迈克尔·斯科特的，我们收到一个粉丝提问，我也对此非常好奇。

967
00:47:25.280 --> 00:47:27.460
It's from Emily V in Kansas.
来自堪萨斯州的艾米丽·V。

968
00:47:27.460 --> 00:47:33.220
And she says, how did the original casting call announcement describe the role of Michael Scott?
她说，最初的选角公告是怎么描述迈克尔·斯科特这个角色的？

969
00:47:33.440 --> 00:47:36.100
Well, Emily Allison was very excited to get this question.
嗯，艾米丽·艾莉森对收到这个问题感到非常兴奋。

970
00:47:36.300 --> 00:47:39.260
She said, oh, Ange, I can find my notes for that.
她说，噢，安吉，我能找到我当时的笔记。

971
00:47:39.400 --> 00:47:42.720
And then she gave like five exclamation points, smiley face.
然后她发了五个感叹号和一个笑脸。

972
00:47:42.880 --> 00:47:44.180
And here's what she wrote.
这是她写的内容。

973
00:47:44.180 --> 00:47:47.180
She said her notes were pretty simple for the role.
她说她关于这个角色的笔记非常简单。

974
00:47:47.460 --> 00:47:50.440
They said, male, age range, 35 to 45.
上面写着：男性，年龄范围35到45岁。

975
00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:58.880
And for character description, it simply said, the manager at a small paper company, Michael, is a bit of a jerk with no self-awareness.
关于角色描述，只写了：一家小型造纸公司的经理，迈克尔，是个有点混蛋且毫无自知之明的人。

976
00:47:59.320 --> 00:47:59.840
Wow.
哇。

977
00:48:00.100 --> 00:48:00.340
Yeah.
是啊。

978
00:48:00.900 --> 00:48:02.880
They threw out a pretty wide net.
他们的选角范围撒得相当广。

979
00:48:03.140 --> 00:48:03.340
Yeah.
是啊。

980
00:48:03.760 --> 00:48:08.980
I always love the little trivia that like Rainn Wilson first auditioned for Michael.
我一直很喜欢那种小花絮，比如雷恩·威尔森最初是为迈克尔这个角色试镜的。

981
00:48:09.140 --> 00:48:09.400
Right.
没错。

982
00:48:09.400 --> 00:48:13.240
Because how different the part would have been if Rainn played Michael.
因为如果由雷恩来演迈克尔，这个角色会有多大的不同啊。

983
00:48:13.460 --> 00:48:13.960
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

984
00:48:14.280 --> 00:48:14.520
Right?
对吧？

985
00:48:14.740 --> 00:48:16.980
I mean, you can only imagine him as Dwight Schrute.
我的意思是，你只能想象他演德怀特·舒鲁特的样子。

986
00:48:17.200 --> 00:48:19.260
But what about some other people?
但其他人呢？

987
00:48:19.420 --> 00:48:21.300
I think about like Ben Falcone.
我想到了本·法尔科内。

988
00:48:22.100 --> 00:48:23.000
Auditioned for Michael.
他为迈克尔试镜过。

989
00:48:23.300 --> 00:48:24.300
Auditioned for Michael.
他也为迈克尔试镜过。

990
00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:33.560
It's so crazy to me when you go through these audition processes and how you hone in on a character and then who ends up playing them.
对我来说，当你经历这些试镜过程，看到你是如何锁定一个角色，以及最后是谁来扮演他们时，这真是太疯狂了。

991
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:37.820
Because in hindsight, I can't imagine anyone but Steve Carell.
因为事后看来，我无法想象除了史蒂夫·卡瑞尔之外的任何人。

992
00:48:38.460 --> 00:48:39.700
He's just perfect.
他简直太完美了。

993
00:48:40.600 --> 00:48:44.320
Well, Angela, we also got this fan question from Jada N.
嗯，安吉拉，我们还收到了来自加利福尼亚州贾达·N的粉丝提问，她说，

994
00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:46.080
in California who said,
“我想知道，珍娜和安吉拉，你们认为哪一幕最能体现迈克尔与安吉拉，以及迈克尔与帕姆之间的关系？”

995
00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:56.260
I'm wondering what scene Jenna and Angela do you think perfectly embodies the relationship between Michael and Angela and Michael and Pam?
噢，这真是个好问题。

996
00:48:57.860 --> 00:48:59.580
Oh, it's such a good question.
你知道，我脑海中浮现出的一个场景，可能不是大家会想到的，但实际上是在圣诞节那一集里，安吉拉在给迈克尔缝裤脚。

997
00:49:01.520 --> 00:49:12.780
You know, one of the ones that comes to mind for me is maybe not one that people would think, but it's actually in the Christmas episode where Angela's hemming Michael's pants.
好的。

998
00:49:13.060 --> 00:49:13.580
Okay.
因为我确实觉得她会帮他处理这类小事，你知道，他可能会为了这类不同的事情去找安吉拉和帕姆。

999
00:49:15.970 --> 00:49:27.310
Because I do feel like that she like helped him with little things like that, you know, that he would probably go to Angela and Pam for different things like that.
当然，我也很喜欢他因为斯普林克尔（猫）伤心欲绝的那一幕。

1000
00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:34.210
And I also, of course, loved when he was heartbroken about sprinkles.
当然，我也很喜欢他因为斯普林克尔伤心欲绝的那一幕。

1001
00:49:34.930 --> 00:49:35.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1002
00:49:35.070 --> 00:49:36.370
He was like, oh, no.
他当时就那种，噢，不。

1003
00:49:37.010 --> 00:49:42.750
You know, he was one of the people that showed true emotion about Angela's cat passing away.
你知道，他是少数几个对安吉拉的猫去世表现出真情实感的人之一。

1004
00:49:43.010 --> 00:49:43.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1005
00:49:43.350 --> 00:49:44.810
I mean, he did get the name wrong.
我是说，他确实把名字叫错了。

1006
00:49:45.190 --> 00:49:47.190
But his emotion was genuine.
但他的感情是真挚的。

1007
00:49:47.710 --> 00:49:47.870
It is emotion, yes.
那是感情，没错。

1008
00:49:48.090 --> 00:49:48.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1009
00:49:49.010 --> 00:49:49.770
That's true.
确实如此。

1010
00:49:50.870 --> 00:49:56.010
Well, I think for me, it would be the scene where Pam finds out that Michael is dating her mom.
嗯，我觉得对我来说，应该是帕姆发现迈克尔在和她妈妈约会的那一幕。

1011
00:49:56.910 --> 00:49:58.530
Yes, that's such a good scene.
没错，那场戏太棒了。

1012
00:49:58.530 --> 00:50:09.530
And the reason is because when she first comes in the office, she is like genuinely invested and excited about his personal life and his relationship.
原因在于，当她刚走进办公室时，她是真心实意地关心并为他的个人生活和恋情感到兴奋。

1013
00:50:09.530 --> 00:50:11.710
And you see their friendship.
你能看到他们的友谊。

1014
00:50:11.710 --> 00:50:13.450
You see the way that they connect.
你能看到他们交流的方式。

1015
00:50:13.450 --> 00:50:18.370
And then by the end of the scene, she finds out who he is dating.
然后到了那场戏的结尾，她发现了他在和谁约会。

1016
00:50:19.010 --> 00:50:21.050
And she is absolutely horrified.
她简直被吓坏了。

1017
00:50:21.230 --> 00:50:28.950
And I just feel like that turn, that whole journey of that scene perfectly embodies the Pam-Michael relationship.
我觉得那种转折，整场戏的整个过程，完美地体现了帕姆和迈克尔的关系。

1018
00:50:28.950 --> 00:50:35.370
It's just like a combination of horror and bonding, I guess.
我想，那就像是恐惧与羁绊的结合体。

1019
00:50:35.570 --> 00:50:35.830
Right?
对吧？

1020
00:50:36.370 --> 00:50:36.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1021
00:50:36.770 --> 00:50:37.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1022
00:50:37.870 --> 00:50:39.190
I love that question.
我喜欢这个问题。

1023
00:50:39.810 --> 00:50:45.390
Well, and, you know, we also asked people to reach out to us if they had a boss like Michael Scott.
嗯，你知道，我们也曾邀请大家，如果他们有像迈克尔·斯科特那样的老板，可以联系我们。

1024
00:50:45.390 --> 00:50:47.210
We said, we want to hear about it.
我们说，我们想听听他们的故事。

1025
00:50:47.990 --> 00:50:50.610
And we got more letters than I was expecting.
结果收到的来信比我预期的要多。

1026
00:50:50.610 --> 00:50:53.410
A lot of people have a boss like Michael Scott.
很多人都有像迈克尔·斯科特那样的老板。

1027
00:50:54.030 --> 00:51:01.170
I don't know if I ever shared with you that I had a coworker that was my personal Michael Scott.
我不知道有没有跟你分享过，我以前有个同事就是我现实生活中的迈克尔·斯科特。

1028
00:51:01.610 --> 00:51:06.010
And it was at the job that I had right before I auditioned for the office.
那是在我参加《办公室》试镜之前的那份工作里。

1029
00:51:06.150 --> 00:51:09.950
And I would imagine this person during my audition process.
在试镜过程中，我脑子里想的就是这个人。

1030
00:51:10.350 --> 00:51:11.710
What were they like?
他是什么样的？

1031
00:51:12.170 --> 00:51:14.150
They were an aspiring comedian.
他是个立志成为喜剧演员的人。

1032
00:51:14.390 --> 00:51:15.590
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1033
00:51:15.590 --> 00:51:22.370
And my desk was right next to the, like, break room.
我的办公桌就在休息室旁边。

1034
00:51:23.470 --> 00:51:31.910
And so in order to, like, go see what the treat of the day was or to refill your coffee, you walked right past my desk.
所以为了去看看当天的零食是什么，或者去续杯咖啡，你必须经过我的办公桌。

1035
00:51:32.450 --> 00:51:42.030
And this guy would chat me up every day with some new pun or some joke that I knew was probably going to be in his stand-up.
那家伙每天都会跟我搭讪，讲些新的双关语或笑话，我知道那些很可能都会出现在他的单口喜剧里。

1036
00:51:42.670 --> 00:51:46.690
And I had to do a lot of Pam-like things.
我不得不做很多像帕姆那样的事。

1037
00:51:47.150 --> 00:51:51.030
You know, he wasn't my boss, but he was a superior.
你知道，他不是我的老板，但他是上级。

1038
00:51:52.010 --> 00:51:57.310
And so I remember that feeling of just being kind of trapped.
所以我记得那种感觉，就像被困住了一样。

1039
00:51:57.510 --> 00:51:57.750
Right.
没错。

1040
00:51:57.950 --> 00:51:58.910
By a person.
被一个人困住了。

1041
00:51:59.250 --> 00:51:59.450
Right.
没错。

1042
00:51:59.730 --> 00:52:06.550
And I remember, like, looking around the office and, like, wondering, like, I wonder if another desk could become available.
我记得我当时环顾办公室，心想，不知道有没有别的办公桌空出来。

1043
00:52:06.550 --> 00:52:10.550
Because I really am, I am, I was in a high traffic area.
因为我真的，我当时处在一个高人流量的区域。

1044
00:52:10.550 --> 00:52:10.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1045
00:52:11.010 --> 00:52:14.830
Well, you know, it's the combination of comedy bits plus trapped audience.
嗯，你知道，这就是喜剧段子加上被困住的观众的结合。

1046
00:52:15.070 --> 00:52:15.310
Yes.
没错。

1047
00:52:15.530 --> 00:52:16.490
Yes, exactly.
是的，完全正确。

1048
00:52:17.590 --> 00:52:22.310
Lady, this is reminding me so much of this last Southwest Airlines flight I was on.
天哪，这让我想起了我上次坐西南航空航班的经历。

1049
00:52:22.490 --> 00:52:22.870
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1050
00:52:23.110 --> 00:52:25.090
Speaking of a trapped audience.
说到被困住的观众。

1051
00:52:25.230 --> 00:52:25.710
Yes.
